From: logos-node-android
Subject: [PATCH 0002] The HTTP API on a Unix socket instead of TCP, when asked for

Against logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain tag 0.3.4. Applied with
`git apply -p1` by native/apply-patches.sh. See native/patches/README.md.

On Android any installed app may connect to 127.0.0.1, so the node API's
wallet endpoints (transfer-funds, sign, channel deposit) answer every app on
the phone. With LOGOS_API_UNIX_SOCKET=<path> set for the node process, the
API listens on that socket file (0600, a stale socket from an earlier run is
removed, any other file there is left alone and the start fails) and on no
TCP port. Unset or empty: upstream behaviour. Routes, handlers, wallet logic,
config format and wire format are unchanged. Independent of patch 0001.

